# K03 RECEIVE-OUTPUT (Codex K03-RECEIVE-OUTPUT-20261007-23; LMX_blog/q/q53.md:95-97; docs/LMX_semantics.en.md
# #construction, #dynamic): a computed output -- a receiver's, merge's, a computed number declaration's -- at a named
# Structure's top level is no field of it, stored at its own receiver occurrence, produced when control reaches it.
# The nested-tail spelling, defined and not run: `x: receiveMessage: msg` receives nothing at its definition, so the
# root's own receive takes C main's one letter.  Exit 7; 81 if the definition took it.
x: receiveMessage: msg
receiveMessage: after
if: after = 0
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 81; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 7; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
